# [[ .Name ]]

A [tug](https://github.com/cuonggt/tug) app: Go handlers render [[ .Framework ]] pages
through Inertia, with no API in between.

```sh
tug dev      # run it on http://localhost:8080, rebuilt and reloaded as it changes
tug gen      # write the TypeScript of the pages' props and the routes
tug build    # build it into one binary, frontend included
go test ./...
```

- `main.go`: the server, its pages and routes, and the health check at
  `/up`. A page is declared with `tug.Page[Props]("Name")`, and its
  component is `resources/js/pages/Name.[[ .Component ]]`. Its pages run
  the scripts that carry their nonce alone, by a Content-Security-Policy,
  as `app.html`'s do: what it blocks, the log says.
- `resources/js/app.[[ .Script ]]`: the app in the browser, which `inertia.[[ .Script ]]`
[[- if .SSR ]]
  makes, and `ssr.[[ .Script ]]`, the app on the server. A first visit's page
  renders there first, with Node, which the app runs beside it from the
  SSR build in `ssr/build`; under tug dev, Vite renders it.
[[- else ]]
  makes.
[[- end ]]
- `lang/`: the app's languages, a file each, as `tug lang vi` writes
  `lang/vi.json` with every text the app and its pages say, to translate.
  The binary embeds them, and `APP_LOCALE` is the one a browser gets that
  asks for none of them. A page says its own words with `useLang`, from
  `resources/js/lib/lang.ts`, as the home page does.
- `resources/js/tug`: the TypeScript tug gen writes from the Go types. It
  isn't edited by hand; tug dev and tug build write it again.
- `AGENTS.md`: how to change the app, for a coding agent, its rules, and
  the commands that check a change, which `CLAUDE.md` hands Claude Code.
- `.env`: read by tug dev. `APP_KEY` encrypts the sessions, and a deployed
  app needs one of its own, set in its environment, with `APP_URL`, its
  own address, and `TRUSTED_PROXIES` behind a load balancer; or, on a
  machine of its own, `TLS_DOMAINS`, for the app to serve HTTPS itself,
  with certificates from Let's Encrypt.
[[ if .SSR -]]
- `Dockerfile`: the app as one static binary on a distroless image with
  Node, for the pages it renders on the server, and the certificates of
  `TLS_DOMAINS` on a volume.
[[- else -]]
- `Dockerfile`: the app as one static binary on a distroless image, with
  the certificates of `TLS_DOMAINS` on a volume.
[[- end ]]
